= Discipline

== When Boards Act

#slide[
  === Boards rarely fire a CEO after one bad year.
  #inv("T2")

  - Directors usually wait until a successor is already working inside the firm.

  - Forced departures cluster in the second and third weak years.
]

#slide[
  === Forced turnover follows the stock price, not the accounts.
  #inv("R1")

  - After a 30% drawdown, the chance of a forced exit within 2 years roughly doubles.

  - Earnings misses alone barely move it.
]
